<title>USA: FSA qualifies 11 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 11 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said it has qualified for bond insurance the following 11 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Coachella Valley USD, Calif., $10 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Napa Valley USD, Calif., $4.6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--South San Francisco USD, Calif., $10 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Clinton, Conn., $6.8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Montague Public Schools, Mich., $11.855 million school building and site bonds.</p>
<p>--Hopkinton School District, N.H., $6.992 million school GOs.</p>
<p>--Fair Lawn, N.J., $15.948 million water bonds.</p>
<p>--Hamilton Twp, N.J., $19.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Southampton Town, N.Y., $4.150 million various purpose bonds.</p>
<p>--First Colony Municipal Utility, Texas, $3.310 million</p>
<p>--Washington $125.195 million GO and refunding bonds</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
